    {
      "id": "background",
      "label": "Curiosity across aesthetics and technology",
      "type": "editorial",
      "layout": "reading",
      "extentWU": 2.9,
      "mobileExtentWU": 3.6,
      "text": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "background-title",
            "kind": "highlight",
            "text": "Perhaps that is why I have always been drawn to the space between aesthetics and technology."
          },
          {
            "id": "background-practice",
            "kind": "prose",
            "text": "I studied Communication Design, then built my work across digital products, web design, identity, interfaces, motion, and creative uses of AI and technology."
          },
          {
            "id": "background-curiosity",
            "kind": "prose",
            "text": "At the centre of it is curiosity: how things work, how they feel and how those qualities can strengthen one another."
          },
          {
            "id": "background-technology",
            "kind": "prose",
            "text": "This is what draws me to emerging technology. I see the opportunity for it to play a useful role in people’s lives once it has been deconstructed, made tangible, made visual and made interactive enough to resonate."
          },
          {
            "id": "background-context",
            "kind": "prose",
            "text": "That curiosity has shaped my work with technology start-ups and creative agencies, on ambitious projects across identity, finance, mobility, healthcare and digital products."
          },
          {
            "id": "background-clients",
            "kind": "clients",
            "items": [
              "Yoti",
              "S&P Global",
              "Bentley",
              "SunExpress",
              "McCann",
              "American Heart Association"
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
